Wi-Fi Commands:

␀␀scanap
␀    Description: Start a Wi-Fi access point (AP) scan.
␀    Usage: scanap [seconds]

␀␀␀scansta
␀␀␀␀    Description: Start scanning for Wi-Fi stations (hops channels).
␀␀␀␀    Usage: scansta

␀␀␀␀stopscan
␀␀␀    Description: Stop any ongoing Wi-Fi scan.
␀␀    Usage: stopscan

␀␀␀attack
␀    Description: Launch an attack (e.g., deauthentication attack).
␀                 Supports multiple selected APs when using 'select -a 1,2,3'.
␀␀    Usage: attack -d (deauth) | attack -c (channel switch) | attack -e (EAPOL logoff) | attack -s (SAE flood)
␀␀    Arguments:
␀        -d  : Start deauth attack (supports multiple APs)
␀␀        -c  : Start channel switch attack (supports multiple APs)
␀␀        -e  : Start EAPOL logoff attack
␀␀␀␀        -s  : Start SAE flood attack (ESP32-C5/C6 only)

␀␀␀list
␀␀␀    Description: List Wi-Fi scan results or connected stations.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: list -a | list -s | list -airtags
␀␀␀        -a  : Show access points from Wi-Fi scan
␀␀␀        -s  : List connected stations
␀␀        -airtags: List discovered AirTags

␀beaconspam
␀    Description: Start beacon spam with different modes.
␀␀␀    Usage: beaconspam [OPTION]
␀        -r   : Start random beacon spam
␀␀␀␀        -rr  : Start Rickroll beacon spam
␀␀        -l   : Start AP List beacon spam
␀␀␀        [SSID]: Use specified SSID for beacon spam

␀␀␀␀stopspam
␀␀␀    Description: Stop ongoing beacon spam.
␀    Usage: stopspam

␀␀␀stopdeauth
␀    Description: Stop ongoing deauthentication attack.
␀    Usage: stopdeauth

␀select
␀    Description: Select access point(s), station, or AirTag by index from the scan results.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: select -a <num[,num,...]> | select -s <num> | select -airtag <num>
␀␀        -a      : AP selection index (supports multiple: 1,3,5)
␀␀␀␀        -s      : Station selection index
␀␀        -airtag : AirTag selection index
␀␀␀    Examples:
␀␀        select -a 4      : Select single AP at index 4
␀        select -a 1,3,5  : Select multiple APs at indices 1, 3, and 5

␀scanall
␀␀␀␀    Description: Perform combined AP and Station scan, display results.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: scanall [seconds]

␀␀sweep
␀␀    Description: Full environment sweep - scans WiFi APs, stations, BLE devices
␀␀␀␀                 and saves comprehensive report to SD card.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: sweep [-w wifi_sec] [-b ble_sec]
␀␀␀␀        -w  : WiFi scan duration per phase in seconds (default: 5)
␀        -b  : BLE scan duration per phase in seconds (default: 5)
␀␀    Output: /mnt/ghostesp/sweeps/sweep_N.csv

␀␀congestion
␀    Description: Display Wi-Fi channel congestion chart.
␀␀␀    Usage: congestion

␀    Description: Connects to Specific WiFi Network and saves credentials.
␀␀    Usage: connect <SSID> [Password]

␀␀apcred
␀    Description: Change or reset the GhostNet AP credentials
␀␀␀    Usage: apcred <ssid> <password>
␀␀␀␀           apcred -r (reset to defaults)
␀␀␀        <ssid>     : New SSID for the AP
␀␀␀        <password> : New password (min 8 characters)
␀␀␀        -r        : Reset to default (GhostNet/GhostNet)

␀␀apenable
␀␀␀    Description: Enable or disable the Access Point across reboots
␀    Usage: apenable <on|off>
␀␀␀        on  : Enable the Access Point (requires restart)
␀␀␀        off : Disable the Access Point (requires restart)

␀listenprobes
␀␀␀    Description: Listen for and log probe requests.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: listenprobes [channel] [stop]
␀␀␀        [channel] : Listen on specific channel (1-165), omit for channel hopping
␀␀␀        stop      : Stop probe request listening

␀␀karma
␀␀    Description: Start or stop the Karma attack (responds to probe requests with specified or all SSIDs).
␀␀    Usage: karma start [ssid1 ssid2 ...]
␀␀␀           karma stop
␀␀        start : Begin Karma attack. Optionally specify SSIDs to respond with (default: all known SSIDs).
␀␀␀        stop  : Stop Karma attack.
␀        karma start
␀␀␀␀        karma start FreeWiFi Starbucks
␀        karma stop

␀␀␀␀trackap
␀␀␀␀    Description: track selected ap signal strength (rssi)
␀␀    Usage: trackap
␀    Note: select an ap first with 'select -a <index>'

␀tracksta
␀␀␀    Description: track selected station signal strength (rssi)
␀    Usage: tracksta
␀␀␀␀    Note: select a station first with 'select -s <index>'

␀setcountry
␀    Description: Set the Wi-Fi country code.
␀␀␀    Usage: setcountry <CC>
␀        <CC> : Country code ("01" world-safe) or two-letter ISO (e.g., US)
␀    Supported: 01, AT, AU, BE, BG, BR, CA, CH, CN, CY, CZ, DE, DK, EE, ES, FI, FR, GB, GR, HK, HR, HU,
␀               IE, IN, IS, IT, JP, KR, LI, LT, LU, LV, MT, MX, NL, NO, NZ, PL, PT, RO, SE, SI, SK, TW, US

␀
BLE Commands:

␀␀␀␀blescan
␀␀␀␀    Description: Handle BLE scanning with various modes.
␀␀␀    Usage: blescan [OPTION]
␀␀␀␀        -f   : Start 'Find the Flippers' mode
␀␀        -ds  : Start BLE spam detector
␀        -a   : Start AirTag scanner
␀␀␀␀        -r   : Scan for raw BLE packets
␀␀␀␀        -s   : Stop BLE scanning

␀␀blespam
␀␀␀␀    Description: Start BLE advertisement spam attacks.
␀    Usage: blespam [OPTION]
␀␀␀␀        -apple     : Apple device spam (AirPods, Apple TV, etc.)
␀␀␀        -ms        : Microsoft Swift Pair spam
␀        -samsung   : Samsung Galaxy Watch spam
␀        -google    : Google Fast Pair spam
␀        -random    : Random spam (cycles through all types)
␀␀␀␀        -s         : Stop BLE spam

␀␀␀␀blewardriving
␀␀    Description: Start/Stop BLE wardriving with GPS logging
␀␀␀␀    Usage: blewardriving [-s]
␀␀        -s  : Stop BLE wardriving

␀list -airtags
␀␀    Description: List discovered AirTags
␀␀␀    Usage: list -airtags

␀␀select -airtag <index>

␀␀␀␀chameleon␀␀␀
Chameleon Ultra Commands:

␀␀␀␀chameleon connect [timeout] [pin]
␀␀    Description: Connect to a Chameleon Ultra device via BLE
␀␀␀    Usage: chameleon connect [timeout_seconds] [pin]
␀␀␀        timeout_seconds : Connection timeout (default: 10)
␀        pin            : PIN for authentication (4-6 digits, optional)

␀␀␀␀chameleon disconnect
␀␀␀    Description: Disconnect from the Chameleon Ultra device
␀␀␀␀    Usage: chameleon disconnect

␀␀␀chameleon status
␀␀␀    Description: Check connection status with Chameleon Ultra
␀␀    Usage: chameleon status

␀␀␀chameleon scanhf
␀␀␀    Description: Scan for High Frequency (HF) RFID tags
␀␀␀␀    Usage: chameleon scanhf

␀␀␀chameleon scanlf
␀␀␀    Description: Scan for Low Frequency (LF) RFID tags
␀    Usage: chameleon scanlf

␀␀␀chameleon battery
␀␀    Description: Get battery information from Chameleon Ultra
␀␀    Usage: chameleon battery

␀␀chameleon reader
␀␀␀    Description: Set Chameleon Ultra to reader mode
␀␀␀␀    Usage: chameleon reader

␀␀␀chameleon emulator
␀    Description: Set Chameleon Ultra to emulator mode
␀␀    Usage: chameleon emulator

␀
Communication Commands:

␀␀commdiscovery
    Check discovery status.
    Usage: commdiscovery

␀␀␀␀commconnect
    Connect to a discovered peer ESP32.
    Usage: commconnect <peer_name>
    Example: commconnect ESP_A1B2C3

␀␀␀␀commsend
    Send a command to connected peer ESP32.
    Usage: commsend <command> [data]
    Example: commsend scanap
    Example: commsend hello world

␀␀commstatus
    Show communication status.
    Usage: commstatus

␀␀␀commdisconnect
    Disconnect from current peer.
    Usage: commdisconnect

␀␀␀␀commsetpins
    Change communication GPIO pins at runtime.
    Usage: commsetpins <tx_pin> <rx_pin>
    Example: commsetpins 4 5

␀␀sd␀␀
SD Card Commands:

␀␀␀␀-- File Operations (machine-parsable) --
␀␀␀sd status
    Show SD mount status, type, capacity, usage.
    Usage: sd status

␀␀␀sd list
    List files/dirs with indices.
    Usage: sd list [path]

␀␀␀sd info
    Show file/dir details.
    Usage: sd info <index|path>

␀␀␀␀sd size
    Get file size.
    Usage: sd size <index|path>

␀␀␀␀sd read
    Read file (chunked downloads).
    Usage: sd read <index|path> [offset] [length]

␀␀sd write
    Create/overwrite file with base64 data.
    Usage: sd write <path> <base64>

␀␀sd append
    Append base64 data to file.
    Usage: sd append <path> <base64>

␀␀␀␀sd mkdir
    Create directory.
    Usage: sd mkdir <path>

␀sd rm
    Delete file or empty directory.
    Usage: sd rm <index|path>

␀␀␀sd tree
    Recursive listing.
    Usage: sd tree [path] [depth]

␀␀-- Pin Configuration --
␀␀␀␀sd_config
    Show current SD GPIO pin configuration.
    Usage: sd_config

␀␀␀␀sd_pins_mmc
    Set GPIO pins for SDMMC mode.
    Usage: sd_pins_mmc <clk> <cmd> <d0> <d1> <d2> <d3>

␀␀sd_pins_spi
    Set GPIO pins for SPI mode.
    Usage: sd_pins_spi <cs> <clk> <miso> <mosi>

␀␀␀sd_save_config
    Save pin config to NVS.
    Usage: sd_save_config

␀␀
LED & RGB Commands:

␀␀rgbmode
    Control LED effects (rainbow, police, strobe, knight, off)
    Usage: rgbmode <rainbow|police|strobe|knight|off|color>

␀␀␀␀setrgbpins
    Change RGB LED pins
    Usage: setrgbpins <red> <green> <blue>
           (use same value for all pins for single-pin LED strips)

␀␀setrgbcount
    Configure how many RGB LEDs are attached
    Usage: setrgbcount <1-512>

␀␀␀setneopixelbrightness
    Set maximum neopixel brightness (percent)
    Usage: setneopixelbrightness <0-100>

␀␀getneopixelbrightness
    Show current neopixel max brightness (percent)
    Usage: getneopixelbrightness

␀misc␀␀␀␀
Miscellaneous Commands:

␀␀    Description: Display this help message.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: help [category]

␀␀␀␀chipinfo
␀␀␀    Description: Display chip information including model, revision, and features
␀␀    Usage: chipinfo
␀␀␀␀    Shows:
␀        - Chip model and revision
␀␀        - CPU cores and features
␀␀␀        - Flash size and memory info
␀␀␀        - ESP-IDF version

␀crash
␀␀    Description: Intentionally trigger a crash (for coredump testing).
␀    Usage: crash
␀␀␀    The device will panic and save a coredump to flash; use idf.py coredump-info to inspect.

␀␀coredump [dump|erase]
␀␀    Description: Read or clear coredump in flash.
␀␀    Usage: coredump        - Print summary (partition size, whether coredump present).
␀           coredump dump   - Stream coredump as base64; save to file and run idf.py coredump-info -c <file> on host.
␀␀␀           coredump erase  - Erase coredump partition (clears saved crash).
␀␀␀␀    With device connected, 'idf.py coredump-info' on host shows full panic reason and backtrace.

␀␀timezone
␀␀␀    Description: Set the display timezone for the clock view.
␀␀    Usage: timezone <TZ_STRING>

␀␀␀webauth
␀␀␀␀    Description: Enable/disable web authentication.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: webauth <enable|disable>

␀␀␀pineap
␀    Description: Start/Stop detecting WiFi Pineapples.
␀    Usage: pineap [-s]
␀        -s  : Stop PineAP detection

␀␀␀Port Scanner
␀␀␀    Description: Scan ports on local subnet or specific IP
␀    Usage: scanports local
␀           scanports <IP> [all | start-end]
␀␀␀␀        all  : Scan all ports (1-65535)
␀␀␀␀        start-end : Custom port range (e.g. 80-443)
␀␀␀␀        (no range) : Scan common ports (default)

␀␀scanarp
␀␀␀␀    Description: Perform ARP scan on local network to discover active hosts
␀␀␀␀    Usage: scanarp

␀␀␀␀    Description: Manage NVS stored settings via command line
␀␀␀    Usage: settings <command> [arguments]
␀␀    Commands:
␀␀        list                    - List all available settings
␀␀        get <setting>           - Get current value of a setting
␀␀␀        set <setting> <value>   - Set a setting to a value
␀        reset [setting]         - Reset setting(s) to defaults
␀        help                    - Show settings help
␀␀␀        settings list
␀␀        settings get ap_ssid
␀␀␀        settings set rgb_mode 1
␀␀␀␀        settings reset

␀␀␀␀    Description: View or change the status display idle animation (status OLED only).
␀␀    Usage: statusidle [list|set <life|ghost|starfield|hud|matrix|ghosts|spiral|leaves|bouncing|0|1|2|3|4|5|6|7|8>]

␀␀␀␀gps␀
GPS Commands:

␀␀␀␀gpsinfo
    Show GPS info.
    Usage: gpsinfo [-s]

␀␀␀␀gpspin
    Set GPS RX pin for external GPS module.
    Usage: gpspin <pin>

␀␀␀␀startwd
    Start GPS wardriving.
    Usage: startwd [-s] [--helper] [--channels <csv>]

␀␀␀wigle␀␀␀
WiGLE Commands:

␀␀wigle API <encoded|name:token>
    Set WiGLE API credentials (encoded token or legacy format).

␀␀␀␀wigle auto on/off
    Enable/disable auto-upload.

␀wigle donate on/off
    Enable/disable WiGLE donate flag.

␀wigle show
    Show WiGLE settings.

␀␀␀wigle list
    Show uploaded CSV memory.

␀␀wigle files [page]
    List CSVs in /mnt/ghostesp/gps/ for manual upload.

␀wigle upload <filename>
    Upload a specific CSV file.

␀␀␀wigle upload all
    Upload all pending queue files.

␀␀wigle stats
    Show account stats for current API key.

␀␀␀
Evil Portal Commands:

␀␀␀␀startportal
␀␀␀␀    Description: Start an Evil Portal using a local file or the default embedded page.
␀                 /mnt/ prefix is added automatically to file paths if missing.
␀    Usage: startportal [FilePath] [AP_SSID] [PSK]
␀␀           PSK is optional for an open network.
␀␀␀␀    Use 'default' as the file path for the default Evil Portal.
␀␀␀␀evilportal
␀    Description: Configure Evil Portal HTML content via UART buffer.
␀␀␀    Usage: evilportal -c sethtmlstr
␀␀␀␀    Steps:
␀      1. Run: evilportal -c sethtmlstr
␀      2. Send [HTML/BEGIN] marker over UART
␀␀␀␀      3. Send HTML content over UART
␀␀␀      4. Send [HTML/CLOSE] marker over UART
␀␀␀␀      5. Run startportal (will use buffered HTML)
␀␀stopportal
␀    Description: Stop Evil Portal
␀␀    Usage: stopportal

␀listportals
    List available Evil Portal files.
    Usage: listportals

␀␀printer␀
Printer Commands:

␀␀␀␀powerprinter
␀␀␀    Description: Print Custom Text to a Printer on your LAN (Requires You to Run Connect First)
␀␀␀␀    Usage: powerprinter <Printer IP> <Text> <FontSize> <alignment>
␀    aligment options: CM = Center Middle, TL = Top Left, TR = Top Right, BR = Bottom Right, BL = Bottom Left

␀␀    Print custom text to a network printer.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: powerprinter <Printer IP> <Text> <FontSize> <alignment>

␀␀␀␀cast␀␀␀␀
YouTube Cast Commands:

␀␀␀dialconnect
␀␀␀␀    Description: Cast a Random Youtube Video on all Smart TV's on your LAN (Requires You to Run Connect First)
␀    Usage: dialconnect

␀␀␀␀    Cast a random YouTube video to all smart TVs on your LAN.
␀␀
Capture Commands:

␀␀␀␀capture
␀␀␀␀    Description: Start a WiFi Capture (Requires SD Card or Flipper)
␀␀␀␀    Usage: capture [OPTION]
␀␀␀␀        -probe     : Start Capturing Probe Packets
␀        -beacon    : Start Capturing Beacon Packets
␀␀␀␀        -deauth    : Start Capturing Deauth Packets
␀␀␀␀        -raw       : Start Capturing Raw Packets
␀␀␀        -wps       : Start Capturing WPS Packets and there Auth Type
␀␀␀        -pwn       : Start Capturing Pwnagotchi Packets
␀␀␀␀        -wireshark : Stream raw PCAP to USB/UART for Wireshark
␀                    Usage: capture -wireshark [-c <channel>]
␀␀␀                    -c <channel>: Lock to specific channel (1-%d)
␀␀        -802154    : Start Capturing IEEE 802.15.4 Packets [C5/C6]
␀        -stop      : Stops the active capture

␀    Start a WiFi packet capture.
␀␀␀    Options: -probe, -beacon, -deauth, -raw, -wps, -pwn, -802154, -stop

␀␀␀
Beacon Spam Commands:

␀␀␀␀beaconadd
    Add an SSID to the beacon spam list.
    Usage: beaconadd <SSID>

␀␀␀␀beaconremove
    Remove an SSID from the beacon spam list.
    Usage: beaconremove <SSID>

␀beaconclear
    Clear the beacon spam list.
    Usage: beaconclear

␀␀␀␀beaconshow
    Show the current beacon spam list.
    Usage: beaconshow

␀␀␀beaconspamlist
    Start beacon spamming using the beacon spam list.
    Usage: beaconspamlist

␀␀␀␀
Attack Commands:

␀dhcpstarve
␀    Description: DHCP starvation flood attack
␀␀    Usage: dhcpstarve start [threads]
␀␀           dhcpstarve stop
␀           dhcpstarve display

␀saeflood
␀␀␀    Description: SAE handshake flooding attack (ESP32-C5/C6 only)
␀␀    Usage: saeflood <password> (requires selected WPA3 AP)

␀␀␀␀stopsaeflood
    Stop SAE flood attack.
    Usage: stopsaeflood

␀␀␀saefloodhelp
    Show detailed SAE flood attack help.
    Usage: saefloodhelp

