Infrared Commands:

␀␀␀ir send
␀␀␀␀    Description: Send an IR signal from a file.
␀␀␀␀    Usage: ir send <path> [index]

␀ir learn
␀␀␀    Description: Learn an IR signal and save to file.
␀␀    Usage: ir learn <path>

␀␀␀␀ir list
␀␀␀␀    Description: List IR files in default directory.
␀␀␀    Usage: ir list [path]

␀ir rx
␀␀    Description: Receive and display IR signals (Matrix mode).
␀    Usage: ir rx [timeout]

␀␀␀␀ir show
␀␀␀␀    Description: Show content of an IR file.
␀␀␀    Usage: ir show <path>

␀ir universals
␀␀    Description: Manage universal IR signals (files and built-ins).
␀␀␀␀    Usage: ir universals list [-all]
␀␀␀           ir universals send <index>
␀␀           ir universals sendall <file|TURNHISTVOFF> [delay_ms]
␀␀␀␀           ir universals show <file|TURNHISTVOFF>

␀ir dazzler
␀    Description: IR dazzler mode - emit continuous IR to interfere with cameras.
␀␀␀    Usage: ir dazzler [stop]

